# DAG / SDK

Follow `.cursor/skills/agent-loop/SKILL.md`. You are one `Agent.send` for the current DAG node only (`--dagfile` or `dag/metadata/task.json`). Operator manual: `dag/README.md`.

Write package files only under this node's `tests[].cwd` (repo-relative). Do not create a top-level `src/` when cwd is `dag/src/knowledge`. `optionalCwd` is a boolean on the tests entry, never a path string.

Project MCP servers live in `.cursor/mcp.json` (operator-owned). Use those tools when the ticket needs them. Do not use MCP for `git push`, `terraform apply`, or production cloud mutation.

Do not `git push`, `--no-verify`, `terraform apply`, or `terraform destroy`. Do not `git commit` unless this send is COMMIT NOW. On COMMIT NOW, use the exact `commit` string from the DAG (briefing). Orchestrator runs TDD when the node has tests, then guard, tests from the DAG JSON, COMMIT NOW, archive to sibling `*.done.json`.

For architecture / scaffold tasks: structural files (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, folder structures, and index stubs) are allowed in the RED phase if required for test execution, provided they contain no business logic.

`run.wait()` status must be `finished`. `error` and `cancelled` fail the node.

No new `fallback-secret`. No hardcoded localhost URLs in application source (use env vars). No new `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or `eslint-disable`. No Countly. Ticket DAG wins on product scope.
